abstract: "An ongoing mathematical-physics research program developing a falsifiable test architecture for physical-to-experiential bridge claims. The repository formalizes deterministic and stochastic factorization tests, intervention-resolved causal structure, temporal and multiscale compatibility, finite-data certification, target-provenance non-circularity, target-measurement channel robustness, target-channel identifiability, quantum operational sufficiency tests, adaptive experiment design, and certified calibration and optimization. Proposition 71 proves that targets constructed as functions or descriptor-only channels of the tested physical descriptor satisfy the corresponding bridge or screening-off condition by construction. Proposition 72 adds the noisy-target layer: under an explicit nondifferential target-measurement channel, the observed conditional residual cannot exceed the latent-target residual, measurement can erase a genuine witness, total-variation witness attenuation can be bounded by a channel-stability coefficient, and a conservative finite-sample target-separation certificate follows. Proposition 73 proves, under a declared binary symmetric three-view model, that two heterogeneous views do not identify individual channel stabilities, while three nondegenerate conditionally independent views identify the three stability magnitudes from observable pairwise moments up to a global latent-label orientation; it also gives simultaneous finite-sample stability intervals. The downstream calibration branch includes lower-bounded heterogeneous calibration and exact primal-dual gap decomposition through P70. The current documented theorem frontier is P73. The physical-to-experiential bridge remains open, and the project does not assume that consciousness is a scalar, state of matter, quantum variable, or additional spacetime dimension."
